SUMMARY:Book Talk: History of the Russian Old Believers on Polish Lands: 
 17th–20th Centuries with Jeffrey Holdeman
DESCRIPTION:History of the Russian Old Believers on Polish Lands: 17th&#8
 211\;20th Centuriesis an English translation from the Polish original of 
 Eugeniusz Iwaniec's 1977 extensively researched and sourced book on the R
 ussian Old Believers from the time of the schism in the Russian Orthodox 
 Church in the 1660s. It was published in 2026 by Slavica Publishers. (htt
 ps://slavica.indiana.edu/history-of-the-russian-old-believers-on-polish-l
 ands/)Prof. Jeff Holdeman is the director of undergraduate studies in SLA
 V and holds a PhD in Slavic Linguistics (Ohio State\, 2002). He has been 
 researching Priestless Russian Old Believers and their descendants in the
  eastern US\, Poland\, Lithuania\, Latvia\, Estonia\, Ukraine\, and Belar
 us since 1998.
