SUMMARY:Your DC Moment | Dinner with Ambassador and Professor Lee Feinstein
DESCRIPTION:Attend an exclusive working dinner and strategy session for t
 he Spring 2027 D.C. Global Policy Program. Don't just study global leader
 ship. Put it into practice.  This intimate event is for students interest
 ed in the Hamilton Lugar Spring 2027 residency. It's a working dinner and
  a peek at what a global career actually feels like before you step into 
 it.Why you should attend:Sit at the Table: Engage with a leader who has s
 haped global policy and his international career.  Alumni Insights: Hear 
 from a panel of D.C. Program alumni regarding their on-the-ground experie
 nces.  The Professional Roadmap: Get a technical walkthrough of the Sprin
 g 2027 cycle\, including the January 11 – May 7 residency dates.  Logis
 tics Bridge: Understand how the IU Capital Campus housing works and how t
 he classes work for undergrads\, grad\, and PhD students.  The AgendaI. T
 he Practitioner Perspective: A briefing from Ambassador Lee Feinstein on 
 D.C. professional realities and "tradecraft" skills.II. The Roadmap: A de
 ep dive into the October 15 deadline\, interview sprints (Oct 26–28)\, 
 and the mandatory December 12 orientation.III. Housing &amp\; Classes: Gu
 idance on the Capital Campus residency and the academic courses offered i
 n D.C.IV. Ground Game: Peer-to-peer breakouts and alumni panel discussion
  on commuting\, and professional life in DC.Can't make the full hour? No 
 problem. This is a come-and-go strategy session designed to fit your Thur
 sday schedule.Link to Application: https://iu.co1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/
 SV_bxucZoEtLdi24a (https://iu.co1.qualtrics.com/jfe/form/SV_bxucZoEtLdi24
 aW)________________________________________________________Biography: Amb
 assador &amp\; Professor Lee Feinstein  Ambassador Lee Feinstein is a Sen
 ior Managing Director and the President of McLarty Associates. He previou
 sly served as the U.S. Ambassador to the Republic of Poland and held seni
 or positions at the Department of State\, including Principal Deputy Dire
 ctor and a Member of the Policy Planning Staff. He was the Founding Dean 
 of the Hamilton Lugar School of Global and International Studies at India
 na University from 2014 to 2022. Ambassador Feinstein is a member of the 
 Council on Foreign Relations and the American Academy of Diplomacy\, and 
 holds a JD from Georgetown University Law Center.
