SUMMARY:Korean Rice Cake Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, October 8thAvailable sessions:&#160\;  Session 1: 
 11:00 - 12:30 p.m.  Session 2: 2:00 - 3:30 p.m.At GISB 1060&#160\;355 N E
 agleson Av.  Bloomington 47405  &#160\;  This event is free and open to t
 he public.&#160\;  All materials will be provided.&#160\;  RSVP ONLY  &#1
 60\;About Songpyeon:  Songpyeon (송편) is a traditional Korean treat ma
 de of glutinous rice. It is a type of tteok (떡)\, small rice cakes\, tr
 aditionally eaten during the Korean autumn harvest festival\, Chuseok (�
 �석). Songpyeon symbolizes a full moon and was used for ancestral celebr
 ations along with other foods to show appreciation for the year's harvest
 . Koreans hoped and prayed to help them avoid misfortune.About&#160\;Jenn
 ifer Lee Ban:Jennifer Lee Ban\, also known as Mama Ban\, is the founder o
 f Rice Blossoms\, a modern Korean dessert brand rooted in tradition and w
 ellness. After becoming a new mom\, she struggled to find wholesome snack
 s for her daughters while seeking a creative outlet after stepping away f
 rom her career as a professional interior designer. Her search led her to
  the art of Korean dessert-making\, where she discovered beautifully craf
 ted treats that were both nourishing and deeply meaningful. Mama Ban was 
 drawn to traditional Korean rice cakes for their natural qualities—they
  are gluten-free\, often vegan\, and thoughtfully made. Today\, through R
 ice Blossoms\, she reimagines these time-honored desserts with a modern s
 ensibility\, steaming each one with care and intention.&#160\;  You will 
 be able to take your Songpyeon home!  Light refreshments will be served.&
 #160\;
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><strong>Thursday\, October 8th<br /></str
 ong>Available sessions:&#160\;<br />  Session 1: 11:00 - 12:30 p.m.<br />
   Session 2: 2:00 - 3:30 p.m.</p><p><strong>At GISB 1060&#160\;<br /></st
 rong>355 N Eagleson Av.<br />  Bloomington 47405</p><p style="text-align:
  center\;">  &#160\;</p><p style="text-align: center\;">  This event is f
 ree and open to the public.&#160\;<br />  All materials will be provided.
 &#160\;<strong><br /><br />  RSVP ONLY</strong></p><p>  &#160\;</p><p><st
 rong>About Songpyeon:</strong><br />  Songpyeon (송편) is a traditional
  Korean treat made of glutinous rice. It is a type of tteok (떡)\, small
  rice cakes\, traditionally eaten during the Korean autumn harvest festiv
 al\, Chuseok (추석). Songpyeon symbolizes a full moon and was used for 
 ancestral celebrations along with other foods to show appreciation for th
 e year's harvest. Koreans hoped and prayed to help them avoid misfortune.
 </p><p><strong>About&#160\;</strong><strong>Jennifer Lee Ban:<br /></stro
 ng>Jennifer Lee Ban\, also known as Mama Ban\, is the founder of Rice Blo
 ssoms\, a modern Korean dessert brand rooted in tradition and wellness. A
 fter becoming a new mom\, she struggled to find wholesome snacks for her 
 daughters while seeking a creative outlet after stepping away from her ca
 reer as a professional interior designer. Her search led her to the art o
 f Korean dessert-making\, where she discovered beautifully crafted treats
  that were both nourishing and deeply meaningful. Mama Ban was drawn to t
 raditional Korean rice cakes for their natural qualities—they are glute
 n-free\, often vegan\, and thoughtfully made. Today\, through Rice Blosso
 ms\, she reimagines these time-honored desserts with a modern sensibility
 \, steaming each one with care and intention.&#160\;</p><p style="text-al
 ign: center\;"><br />  You will be able to take your Songpyeon home!<br /
 >  Light refreshments will be served.&#160\;</p>
