SUMMARY:Academy of Teaching Scholars: Best Practices in Global Health Edu
 cation
DESCRIPTION:Global health education requires intentional curricular desig
 n that addresses cultural humility\, equity\, and reciprocal partnership.
  This workshop\, presented by Dr. Jenny Baenziger\, associate director of
  education for the IU Center for Global Health\, introduces participants 
 to evidence-based approaches for preparing learners to work effectively a
 nd ethically in global health contexts. Special attention is given to avo
 iding extractive educational models and centering the priorities of partn
 er communities.Learning ObjectivesArticulate core competencies and ethica
 l principles that should underpin global health curricula.  Evaluate glob
 al health educational experiences for equity\, bidirectionality\, and cul
 tural responsiveness.  Design or revise learning objectives and preparato
 ry activities that promote safe\, ethical\, and effective global health p
 ractice.  This event aligns with the following IUSM Academy of Teaching S
 cholars program competencies: Learning Theory (L) Meeting URL: https://go
 .iu.edu/nWrj6N
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Global health education requires intent
 ional curricular design that addresses cultural humility\, equity\, and r
 eciprocal partnership. This workshop\, presented by Dr. Jenny Baenziger\,
  associate director of education for the IU Center for Global Health\, in
 troduces participants to evidence-based approaches for preparing learners
  to work effectively and ethically in global health contexts. Special att
 ention is given to avoiding extractive educational models and centering t
 he priorities of partner communities.</p><p><strong><em>Learning Objectiv
 es</em></strong></p><ul><li>Articulate core competencies and ethical prin
 ciples that should underpin global health curricula.  </li><li>Evaluate g
 lobal health educational experiences for equity\, bidirectionality\, and 
 cultural responsiveness.  </li><li>Design or revise learning objectives a
 nd preparatory activities that promote safe\, ethical\, and effective glo
 bal health practice.  </li></ul><p><em>This event aligns with the followi
 ng IUSM Academy of Teaching Scholars program competencies: Learning Theor
 y (L)</em></p> Meeting URL: https://go.iu.edu/nWrj6N
