 East Policy Council.</p><p data-path-to-node="16">  No scripted presentat
 ions or generic advice—just real tradecraft from someone who has manage
 d war-zone evacuations under fire and negotiated at the highest levels of
  national security.</p><h4 data-path-to-node="17">  Who Can Attend?</h4><
 p data-path-to-node="18">  Open to all: Students (Undergrad &amp\; Grad)\
 , Faculty\, Staff\, and the Public. <i data-path-to-node="18" data-index-
 in-node="74">(Catered dinner provided)</i></p><h4 data-path-to-node="19">
   What You'll Get Out of It</h4><ul data-path-to-node="20"><li><p data-pa
 th-to-node="20\,0\,0">      Unfiltered Access: Direct\, small-group face 
 time with a senior diplomat who operated across the State Department\, De
 fense Department\, and National Security Council.    </p></li><li><p data
 -path-to-node="20\,1\,0">      Crisis Tradecraft: Real-world lessons on h
 igh-pressure decision-making\, from counterterrorism networks to cyber wa
 rfare and emergency evacuations.    </p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="20
 \,2\,0">      Insider Career Strategy: The exact playbook for breaking in
 to national security\, intelligence\, foreign policy\, and top internatio
 nal fellowships.    </p></li><li><p data-path-to-node="20\,3\,0">      Ra
 w Answers: Bring your real questions about power dynamics\, navigating fe
 deral bureaucracy\, and building leverage early in your career.    </p></
 li></ul><h3 data-path-to-node="22">  Bio: Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Win
 stanley</h3><p data-path-to-node="23">  Ambassador Gina Abercrombie-Winst
 anley is a 30-year diplomat\, former U.S. Ambassador to the Republic of M
 alta\, and President of the Middle East Policy Council. Her career spans 
 executive leadership roles across the Department of State\, Defense Depar
 tment\, National Security Council\, and Senate Foreign Relations Committe
 e. She has advised the commander of U.S. cyber forces on foreign policy p
 riorities\, expanded international counterterrorism partnerships as Deput
 y Coordinator for Counterterrorism\, and led the emergency evacuation of 
 thousands of U.S. citizens from a war zone. She is a recipient of the Sta
 te Department Superior Honor Award for acts of courage during an al-Qaeda
  attack on the U.S. Consulate in Jeddah.</p>
